WEBVTT

1.1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.740
Welcome to Survive Drive. Set a trip, compare candidate

1.2
00:00:03.740 --> 00:00:07.480
routes, inspect the evidence, and choose for yourself. The

1.3
00:00:07.480 --> 00:00:11.220
app organizes information; it does not declare a route

1.4
00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:15.375
safe. This tour shows the controls and why they exist.

2.1
00:00:16.075 --> 00:00:19.398
Most of this machinery exists to keep AVM lookups

2.2
00:00:19.398 --> 00:00:23.459
economical. A cell can be shared by several routes, and a

2.3
00:00:23.459 --> 00:00:27.151
saved value can be reused without a new RentCast request.

2.4
00:00:27.151 --> 00:00:30.843
At one cent per new lookup, ten million uncached lookups

2.5
00:00:30.843 --> 00:00:33.797
would total one hundred thousand dollars. A nationwide

2.6
00:00:33.797 --> 00:00:37.120
prefill could reach or exceed that scale, depending on

2.7
00:00:37.120 --> 00:00:40.812
grid density. SD focuses on the cells relevant to your

2.8
00:00:40.812 --> 00:00:41.550
trip instead.

3.1
00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.537
Enter coordinates or place the start and destination on

3.2
00:00:45.537 --> 00:00:49.554
the map. You can name each point, choose faster travel or

3.3
00:00:49.554 --> 00:00:53.205
a balance of time and distance, and set road preferences

3.4
00:00:53.205 --> 00:00:56.127
such as highways and tolls. These preferences guide

3.5
00:00:56.127 --> 00:00:59.779
Valhalla; avoid does not guarantee that a road type will

3.6
00:00:59.779 --> 00:01:02.700
disappear. This version does not use live traffic.

4.1
00:01:03.400 --> 00:01:06.956
Escape Gates offer possible approaches near both ends of

4.2
00:01:06.956 --> 00:01:10.907
the trip. Adjust the ring and gate settings, then select

4.3
00:01:10.907 --> 00:01:14.462
GO to find road suggestions. Review the gates before

4.4
00:01:14.462 --> 00:01:18.018
searching. With sixteen gates at each end, including the

4.5
00:01:18.018 --> 00:01:21.574
no-gate cases, the full cross product is seventeen by

4.6
00:01:21.574 --> 00:01:24.339
seventeen, or two hundred eighty-nine Valhalla requests.

4.7
00:01:24.339 --> 00:01:27.500
The exact batch is shown before the search.

5.1
00:01:28.200 --> 00:01:31.964
The route budget shows the prepared Valhalla requests and

5.2
00:01:31.964 --> 00:01:35.310
provider-attempt count. When the local Valhalla service is

5.3
00:01:35.310 --> 00:01:38.656
ready, the prepared batch starts automatically within that

5.4
00:01:38.656 --> 00:01:42.420
limit. A failed request stops the workflow for review.

5.5
00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:46.184
There is no automatic Valhalla retry. The route search

5.6
00:01:46.184 --> 00:01:48.275
does not spend AVM credits.

6.1
00:01:48.975 --> 00:01:52.792
Evaluate first maps eligible route cells and checks saved

6.2
00:01:52.792 --> 00:01:56.609
AVM values. Round zero ranks with that known evidence

6.3
00:01:56.609 --> 00:02:00.426
before asking for new paid lookups. Its default cutoff

6.4
00:02:00.426 --> 00:02:03.395
deactivates thirty-five percent of the nominal candidates,

6.5
00:02:03.395 --> 00:02:07.212
while routes with less than twenty percent known coverage

6.6
00:02:07.212 --> 00:02:11.029
are protected. Unknown cells remain unknown; they are not

6.7
00:02:11.029 --> 00:02:12.725
treated as low values.

7.1
00:02:13.425 --> 00:02:17.205
Each candidate shows its rank, known coverage, and unknown

7.2
00:02:17.205 --> 00:02:20.565
cells. INCLUDED means eligible for the next evidence

7.3
00:02:20.565 --> 00:02:23.925
round; EXCLUDED candidates remain visible and can return

7.4
00:02:23.925 --> 00:02:27.705
after reranking. The Red cutoff classifies known cells by

7.5
00:02:27.705 --> 00:02:31.905
price per square foot. This is a geographic value signal,

7.6
00:02:31.905 --> 00:02:35.685
not a measured safety rating. Highway runs and attached

7.7
00:02:35.685 --> 00:02:38.625
ramps are left out of AVM evaluation.

8.1
00:02:39.325 --> 00:02:43.090
For more evidence, choose the number of new cells per

8.2
00:02:43.090 --> 00:02:46.479
INCLUDED route. SD checks the shared cache and removes

8.3
00:02:46.479 --> 00:02:49.492
duplicate cells across routes. Calculate exact One Round

8.4
00:02:49.492 --> 00:02:53.257
lookups to see the final new-call count before you select

8.5
00:02:53.257 --> 00:02:57.775
Run. Each new lookup is counted as one credit at one cent

8.6
00:02:57.775 --> 00:03:01.164
in the current cost display. Failed attempts count, and

8.7
00:03:01.164 --> 00:03:03.800
paid provider calls are not retried automatically.

9.1
00:03:04.500 --> 00:03:09.033
Set the Red threshold for ranking and the upper map-color

9.2
00:03:09.033 --> 00:03:12.205
bound for visual contrast. Changing these settings

9.3
00:03:12.205 --> 00:03:15.832
reclassifies or recolors saved evidence without buying new

9.4
00:03:15.832 --> 00:03:19.004
values. Colored cells describe estimated property value

9.5
00:03:19.004 --> 00:03:23.990
around a route, not danger or safety. A missing AVM value

9.6
00:03:23.990 --> 00:03:25.350
still means unknown.

10.1
00:03:26.050 --> 00:03:29.879
Open Street View from a map point and check when the

10.2
00:03:29.879 --> 00:03:33.012
imagery was taken. Record what you notice separately from

10.3
00:03:33.012 --> 00:03:36.493
the AVM signal. Then compare route trade-offs and choose a

10.4
00:03:36.493 --> 00:03:39.975
candidate. Export the session or decision if you want a

10.5
00:03:39.975 --> 00:03:43.804
copy. You remain in control of the route and every new

10.6
00:03:43.804 --> 00:03:44.500
evidence round.
